.\" Manpage for mkex

.TH MKEX 1 "July 26, 2026" "mkex 2.2" "Development Utility Manuals"
.SH NAME
\fBmkex\fR \- create an executable file with an interpreter line and open it
in an editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmkex\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fP] \fIFILE\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmkex\fR creates \fIFILE\fP, adds executable permissions, writes an
interpreter line for the chosen language, and opens the file in an editor.
This can also trigger syntax highlighting in editors that infer file type from
the interpreter line.
.PP
If \fB-I\fR is used with \fBbash\fR, \fBsh\fR, or \fBzsh\fR, \fBmkex\fR
writes an \fBIFS=$'\\n'\fR line beneath the interpreter line.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP "\fB-e \fIEDITOR\fR"
Choose the editor to open the file in.
If this option is not used, \fBmkex\fR checks \fB$FCEDIT\fR,
\fB$VISUAL\fR, and \fB$EDITOR\fR, in that order.
If none are set, it defaults to \fBvim\fR.
.IP "\fB-E \fIPERMS\fR"
Set permissions for the created file.
By default, permissions are set to \fB755\fR.
Permissions must be a three-digit chmod-style value, such as \fB755\fR or
\fB700\fR, and the owner must have execute permission.
.IP "\fB-o \fIOPTION\fR"
Add an option after the interpreter line.
For example, \fB-o -x\fR can be used with \fBbash\fR.
.IP "\fB-C\fR"
Clobber.
If \fIFILE\fR exists, overwrite it without asking.
.IP "\fB-B\fR"
No-clobber.
If \fIFILE\fR exists, report an error and exit.
.IP "\fB-O\fR"
Prompt before overwriting an existing file.
This is the default and is useful for overriding \fBmode=clobber\fR in
\fB~/.mkexrc\fR.
.IP "\fB-I\fR"
Write \fBIFS=$'\\n'\fR below the interpreter line.
This option is accepted only with \fBbash\fR, \fBsh\fR, and \fBzsh\fR.
.IP "\fB-n\fR"
Use \fB/usr/bin/env \fILANGUAGE\fR instead of resolving the interpreter path
immediately.
.IP "\fB-N\fR"
Unset a configured \fBenv=true\fR option from \fB~/.mkexrc\fR.
.IP "\fB-V\fR"
Print version information and exit.
.IP "\fB-u\fR"
Display usage.
.IP "\fB-h\fR"
Display short help.
.SH LANGUAGE OPTIONS
One language option is required unless \fBlang\fR is configured in
\fB~/.mkexrc\fR.
.IP "\fB-l \fILANGUAGE\fR"
Choose \fILANGUAGE\fR by name.
For common languages, single-letter options are available.
.IP "\fB-i \fIINTERPRETER\fR"
Use a custom interpreter path.
Pass only the path; \fBmkex\fR adds \fB#!\fR automatically.
.IP "\fB-r\fR"
ruby
.IP "\fB-b\fR"
bash
.IP "\fB-a\fR"
awk
.IP "\fB-d\fR"
sed
.IP "\fB-z\fR"
zsh
.IP "\fB-f\fR"
fish
.IP "\fB-s\fR"
sh
.IP "\fB-c\fR"
csh
.IP "\fB-k\fR"
ksh
.IP "\fB-K\fR"
krsh
.IP "\fB-p\fR"
python
.IP "\fB-P\fR"
php
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP "\fBFCEDIT\fR"
First editor fallback checked when \fB-e\fR is not passed.
.IP "\fBVISUAL\fR"
Second editor fallback checked when \fB-e\fR is not passed.
.IP "\fBEDITOR\fR"
Third editor fallback checked when \fB-e\fR is not passed.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILES
\fBmkex\fR accepts a configuration file at \fB~/.mkexrc\fR.
Available variables are:
.PP
.nf
lang=LANGUAGE
perms=PERMISSIONS
editor=EDITOR
env=true
clobber=true
setifs=true
mode=clobber
mode=noclobber
mode=interactive
.fi
.PP
Boolean values are false by default.
Command-line flags override configuration values where an override exists.
For example, \fB-N\fR unsets configured \fBenv=true\fR, and \fB-O\fR
restores the interactive overwrite prompt.
